{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he shall bear his iniquity.</b> Always: 'and He will forgive his iniquity' — through the punishment that HaShem brings upon him. And because he mentioned the matters of the goats that they used to perform in Egypt, this pericope and the forbidden sexual relations were juxtaposed to 'the deeds of the land of Canaan,' for so it is explicitly stated at the end."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:35.710731014Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}